  "observations": [
    "Element stride1120; array pointer+8, count+0x10, capacity+0x14. New capacity starts4, doubles through ordinary history sizes; large-count increment is min(count,0x3a842) beyond the byte threshold0x10000000.",
    "SetCapacity growth reallocates existing bytes, zeros new tail and default-constructs every new capacity slot. It does not call view copy constructors/assignments for retained elements. Shrink/destruction destroys capacity elements in reverse order.",
    "Append(source) increments count then invokes view assignment on a preconstructed slot. A full-capacity source alias uses a default temporary + assignment, reserve, then final assignment and temporary destruction.",
    "AppendNew recreates an unused existing capacity slot; newly grown default slots are returned directly.",
    "Remove(index) destroys selected view, clears bytes, moves tail with memmove, clears/reconstructs old last slot, then decrements count. RemoveLast delegates with count-1. Empty destroys/reconstructs active slots in reverse and retains capacity.",
    "Original raw move/resize addresses are not portable. Managed implementation keeps safe logical owner references, preserves values/copy counts and does not claim native dangling-pointer/address alias equivalence.",
    "Fresh view defaults are grounded in original constructor/default/viewport initialize and construction-plane/page/trace helpers. Shared XY plane resides in non-file-backed data and is initialized by a no-input runtime initializer calling CreateFromFrame(origin0,X1,Y1). Plane equation Create negates the zero dot product, yielding negative-zero D."
  ],
